    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        ":::: {.callout-warning icon=\"false\"}\n",
        "## 🧠 Pregunta\n",
        "\n",
        "¿La variable respuesta parece simétrica?  \n",
        "¿Observas algún comportamiento particular en los valores más altos?\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.callout-tip collapse=\"true\" icon=\"false\"}\n",
        "## Solución\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "Este conjunto contiene dos variables especialmente interesantes:\n",
        "\n",
        "- `Latitude`\n",
        "- `Longitude`\n",
        "\n",
        "que permiten visualizar aproximadamente la distribución espacial de las observaciones.\n"
      ],
      "id": "9c3f5505"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "plt.figure(figsize=(8, 6))\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.scatter(\n",
        "    X[\"Longitude\"],\n",
        "    X[\"Latitude\"],\n",
        "    c=y,\n",
        "    s=8,\n",
        "    alpha=0.5\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.xlabel(\"Longitude\")\n",
        "plt.ylabel(\"Latitude\")\n",
        "plt.title(\"Distribución geográfica de las observaciones\")\n",
        "plt.colorbar(label=\"Valor mediano de la vivienda\")\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "f27c1e6a",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "La localización contiene información potencialmente importante para predecir el valor de las viviendas.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Separación de los datos\n",
        "\n",
        "Antes de comenzar a probar modelos, reservaremos una parte de los datos para realizar una evaluación final.\n",
        "\n",
        "Utilizaremos $80\\%$ de las observaciones para entrenamiento y reservaremos el $20\\%$ restante para prueba."
      ],
      "id": "72bf8fcc"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(\n",
        "    X,\n",
        "    y,\n",
        "    test_size=0.20,\n",
        "    random_state=42\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "5f4d9e45",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Revisemos las dimensiones."
      ],
      "id": "fc20cc02"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "print(\"X_train:\", X_train.shape)\n",
        "print(\"X_test: \", X_test.shape)"
      ],
      "id": "7512a273",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "::: {.callout-important}\n",
        "## El conjunto de prueba se reserva\n",
        "\n",
        "A partir de este momento trabajaremos principalmente con `X_train` y `y_train`.\n",
        "\n",
        "El conjunto de prueba representa datos que el modelo no debe utilizar durante el proceso de entrenamiento y selección.\n",
        "\n",
        "En las siguientes clases veremos con mayor detalle cómo utilizar **Cross-Validation** para realizar esta selección correctamente.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Una referencia inicial: DummyRegressor\n",
        "\n",
        "Antes de utilizar un modelo más complejo necesitamos una referencia.\n",
        "\n",
        "Un modelo complicado no es necesariamente útil simplemente porque produce predicciones. Debemos preguntarnos si logra mejorar una estrategia extremadamente sencilla.\n",
        "\n",
        "Utilizaremos `DummyRegressor`, que puede predecir siempre la media de la variable respuesta."
      ],
      "id": "1a85b676"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "dummy = DummyRegressor(strategy=\"mean\")\n",
        "\n",
        "dummy.fit(X_train, y_train)"
      ],
      "id": "58cc9795",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Generamos las predicciones sobre el conjunto de entrenamiento."
      ],
      "id": "9d4e1e4f"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "y_pred_dummy = dummy.predict(X_train)"
      ],
      "id": "92054bf1",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Calculamos MAE y RMSE.\n",
        "\n",
        "Recordemos que\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\operatorname{MAE}\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\frac{1}{n}\n",
        "\\sum_{i=1}^{n}\n",
        "|y_i-\\widehat y_i|,\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "mientras que\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\operatorname{RMSE}\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\sqrt{\n",
        "\\frac{1}{n}\n",
        "\\sum_{i=1}^{n}\n",
        "(y_i-\\widehat y_i)^2\n",
        "}.\n",
        "$$"
      ],
      "id": "367f3082"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "mae_dummy = mean_absolute_error(y_train, y_pred_dummy)\n",
        "rmse_dummy = np.sqrt(\n",
        "    mean_squared_error(y_train, y_pred_dummy)\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"MAE:  {mae_dummy:.4f}\")\n",
        "print(f\"RMSE: {rmse_dummy:.4f}\")"
      ],
      "id": "21703d48",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Estos valores constituyen una **baseline** muy sencilla.\n",
        "\n",
        "Nuestro Gradient Boosting debería ser capaz de mejorar claramente esta referencia.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Nuestro primer Gradient Boosting\n",
        "\n",
        "Construyamos ahora un modelo de Gradient Boosting.\n",
        "\n",
        "Comenzaremos con una configuración sencilla:"
      ],
      "id": "fa72b4d8"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "gbr = GradientBoostingRegressor(\n",
        "    n_estimators=100,\n",
        "    learning_rate=0.1,\n",
        "    max_depth=2,\n",
        "    random_state=42\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "e405345f",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Recordemos el significado de estos tres hiperparámetros:\n",
        "\n",
        "| Hiperparámetro | Interpretación |\n",
        "|---|---|\n",
        "| `n_estimators` | Número de árboles construidos secuencialmente |\n",
        "| `learning_rate` | Magnitud de la contribución de cada nuevo árbol |\n",
        "| `max_depth` | Profundidad máxima de cada árbol |\n",
        "\n",
        "Entrenamos el modelo."
      ],
      "id": "bb91375a"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "gbr.fit(X_train, y_train)"
      ],
      "id": "fd4f0ee7",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Y obtenemos las predicciones."
      ],
      "id": "2d2e5431"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "y_pred_train = gbr.predict(X_train)"
      ],
      "id": "9dc79d4a",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Calculamos nuevamente MAE y RMSE."
      ],
      "id": "223afb56"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "mae_gbr = mean_absolute_error(y_train, y_pred_train)\n",
        "\n",
        "rmse_gbr = np.sqrt(\n",
        "    mean_squared_error(y_train, y_pred_train)\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"MAE:  {mae_gbr:.4f}\")\n",
        "print(f\"RMSE: {rmse_gbr:.4f}\")"
      ],
      "id": "a8ecc5c3",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Comparemos con nuestra baseline."
      ],
      "id": "581c6b7a"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "resultados = pd.DataFrame({\n",
        "    \"Modelo\": [\"Dummy\", \"Gradient Boosting\"],\n",
        "    \"MAE\": [mae_dummy, mae_gbr],\n",
        "    \"RMSE\": [rmse_dummy, rmse_gbr]\n",
        "})\n",
        "\n",
        "resultados"
      ],
      "id": "38166e41",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "::: {.callout-note}\n",
        "## Cuidado con la interpretación\n",
        "\n",
        "Por ahora estamos comparando el desempeño sobre los **datos de entrenamiento**.\n",
        "\n",
        "Un menor error de entrenamiento no garantiza que el modelo generalice mejor.\n",
        "\n",
        "En la siguiente clase utilizaremos Cross-Validation para realizar una comparación mucho más adecuada.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## ¿Cómo aprende el ensamble?\n",
        "\n",
        "Una ventaja de `GradientBoostingRegressor` es que podemos observar las predicciones después de cada etapa del ensamble.\n",
        "\n",
        "Nuestro modelo contiene $100$ árboles:"
      ],
      "id": "b5a736b3"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "gbr.n_estimators"
      ],
      "id": "9ec332de",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Con `staged_predict()` podemos obtener las predicciones después de utilizar:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "1,2,3,\\ldots,100\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "árboles.\n",
        "\n",
        "Calcularemos el RMSE después de cada etapa."
      ],
      "id": "a81ed258"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "errores_train = []\n",
        "\n",
        "for y_pred in gbr.staged_predict(X_train):\n",
        "    rmse = np.sqrt(\n",
        "        mean_squared_error(y_train, y_pred)\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    errores_train.append(rmse)"
      ],
      "id": "05ffcad2",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Ahora graficamos el error."
      ],
      "id": "e39c1af0"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "plt.figure(figsize=(8, 5))\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.plot(\n",
        "    range(1, len(errores_train) + 1),\n",
        "    errores_train\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.xlabel(\"Número de árboles\")\n",
        "plt.ylabel(\"RMSE de entrenamiento\")\n",
        "plt.title(\"Evolución del error durante Gradient Boosting\")\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "dcbd6bde",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "¿Qué observamos?\n",
        "\n",
        "A medida que agregamos árboles, el ensamble intenta corregir los errores de los modelos anteriores.\n",
        "\n",
        "En términos generales, el modelo después de $m$ iteraciones tiene la forma\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "F_m(\\mathbf{x})\n",
        "=\n",
        "F_{m-1}(\\mathbf{x})\n",
        "+\n",
        "\\eta h_m(\\mathbf{x}),\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "donde $h_m(\\mathbf{x})$ representa la corrección aprendida por el nuevo árbol y $\\eta$ es el *learning rate*.\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.callout-warning icon=\"false\"}\n",
        "## 🧠 Pregunta\n",
        "\n",
        "¿El error de entrenamiento aumenta o disminuye al agregar árboles? ¿Significa esto que siempre debemos utilizar tantos árboles como sea posible?\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.callout-tip collapse=\"true\" icon=\"false\"}\n",
        "## Solución\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "La segunda pregunta es especialmente importante. El comportamiento sobre entrenamiento no es suficiente para decidir cuántos árboles necesitamos.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Learning rate\n",
        "\n",
        "El hiperparámetro `learning_rate` controla cuánto contribuye cada nuevo árbol al ensamble.\n",
        "\n",
        "La actualización es\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "F_m(\\mathbf{x})\n",
        "=\n",
        "F_{m-1}(\\mathbf{x})\n",
        "+\n",
        "\\eta h_m(\\mathbf{x}).\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Si $\\eta$ es grande, cada árbol puede producir una corrección importante.\n",
        "\n",
        "Si $\\eta$ es pequeño, las correcciones son más conservadoras.\n",
        "\n",
        "Comparemos tres valores:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\eta\\in\\{1,\\;0.1,\\;0.01\\}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Mantendremos inicialmente el mismo número de árboles."
      ],
      "id": "3ee4f1e2"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "learning_rates = [1.0, 0.1, 0.01]\n",
        "\n",
        "modelos_lr = {}\n",
        "\n",
        "for lr in learning_rates:\n",
        "    \n",
        "    modelo = GradientBoostingRegressor(\n",
        "        n_estimators=100,\n",
        "        learning_rate=lr,\n",
        "        max_depth=2,\n",
        "        random_state=42\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    \n",
        "    modelo.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
        "    \n",
        "    modelos_lr[lr] = modelo"
      ],
      "id": "87ffd3c2",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Calculemos el RMSE de entrenamiento."
      ],
      "id": "1fa1b9dc"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "resultados_lr = []\n",
        "\n",
        "for lr, modelo in modelos_lr.items():\n",
        "    \n",
        "    pred = modelo.predict(X_train)\n",
        "    \n",
        "    rmse = np.sqrt(\n",
        "        mean_squared_error(y_train, pred)\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    \n",
        "    resultados_lr.append({\n",
        "        \"learning_rate\": lr,\n",
        "        \"RMSE_train\": rmse\n",
        "    })\n",
        "\n",
        "pd.DataFrame(resultados_lr)"
      ],
      "id": "61324a9b",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Pero resulta más interesante observar cómo evoluciona el error."
