      "source": [
        "::: {.callout-tip}\n",
        "## Learning rate y número de árboles\n",
        "\n",
        "Un `learning_rate` pequeño no significa necesariamente un peor modelo.\n",
        "\n",
        "Significa que cada árbol contribuye menos y, por lo tanto, generalmente necesitaremos **más árboles**.\n",
        "\n",
        "Podemos pensar en la relación\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\text{learning rate pequeño}\n",
        "\\quad\\longrightarrow\\quad\n",
        "\\text{más árboles}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Interacción entre learning rate y número de árboles\n",
        "\n",
        "Hasta ahora fijamos\n",
        "\n",
        "```text\n",
        "n_estimators = 100\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "para todos los modelos.\n",
        "\n",
        "Esto puede ser injusto para un modelo con `learning_rate=0.01`, ya que sus correcciones son mucho más pequeñas.\n",
        "\n",
        "Comparemos diferentes combinaciones."
      ],
      "id": "8367422f"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "configuraciones = [\n",
        "    (1.0, 50),\n",
        "    (0.1, 100),\n",
        "    (0.05, 200),\n",
        "    (0.01, 500)\n",
        "]\n",
        "\n",
        "resultados = []\n",
        "\n",
        "for lr, n_arboles in configuraciones:\n",
        "    \n",
        "    modelo = GradientBoostingRegressor(\n",
        "        n_estimators=n_arboles,\n",
        "        learning_rate=lr,\n",
        "        max_depth=2,\n",
        "        random_state=42\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    \n",
        "    modelo.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
        "    \n",
        "    pred = modelo.predict(X_train)\n",
        "    \n",
        "    rmse = np.sqrt(\n",
        "        mean_squared_error(y_train, pred)\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    \n",
        "    resultados.append({\n",
        "        \"learning_rate\": lr,\n",
        "        \"n_estimators\": n_arboles,\n",
        "        \"RMSE_train\": rmse\n",
        "    })\n",
        "\n",
        "pd.DataFrame(resultados)"
